  "title": "What Rabbinical Judaism put in place of blood sacrifices",
  "summary": "A list of seven things Rabbinical Judaism substituted for blood sacrifices: confess the sin, pray for atonement, correct the sin, pursue works of chesed (kindness) and truth, remember the sin, do not repeat it, and teach others not to sin.",
  "text": [
    {"lang": "en", "role": "heading", "text": "Rabbinical Judaism Replaced Blood Sacrifices with:"},
    {"lang": "en", "role": "list", "text": "Confess the sin"},
    {"lang": "en", "role": "list", "text": "Pray for atonement"},
    {"lang": "en", "role": "list", "text": "Correct the sin however possible"},
    {"lang": "en", "role": "list", "text": "Pursue works of chesed and truth;"},
    {"lang": "en", "role": "list", "text": "Remember the sin for the rest of one's life;"},
    {"lang": "en", "role": "list", "text": "Do not commit same sin if opportunity arises"},
    {"lang": "en", "role": "list", "text": "Teach others not to sin."}
